INT. NIGHT FERRY - CAR DECK - NIGHT

Engines thrum. Six figures around a rusted minivan. INES VARELA, 40s, SEUN ADEYEMI, 30s, HARLAN COOPER-REID, 60s, PRIYA NAIR, 20s, DMITRI SOKOLOV, 50s, and GRANDMA ZOFIA, 80s, in a folding chair.

She clutches an urn. He pretends not to see. They all stare at the lid.

INES
We scatter it at the island, like she said.

HARLAN
She said the harbor.

SEUN
She said both. She said a lot of things.

Zofia laughs at nothing. Priya takes the urn from Ines, gently, and Ines lets go too fast.

PRIYA
(to herself)
Okay. Okay.

DMITRI
Someone opened this.

Silence. He holds up the lid, tape peeled. Harlan studies the floor. Ines reaches for the urn again.

INES
Who opened it?

HARLAN
She asked me to look.

SEUN
(over Harlan)
You looked? You LOOKED?

DMITRI
Seun, quiet.

INES
(over both)
There's nothing in it, is there.

Priya tips the urn. Ash, grey, real. Everyone exhales. Zofia stops laughing.

ZOFIA
That is not Marta.

They turn as one.
